+---
+'@link-assistant/hive-mind': patch
+---
+
+Fix the CI/CD false negatives found on `main` (issue #2625). The dependency-freshness gate now blocks pull requests only and warns on pushes. The fixture cleanup reports ruleset-retained branches as retained, not as errors. `release.yml` can be dispatched with `mode=checks` alone. The Formal AI draft creates its label when it is missing. Log uploads no longer retry a token that cannot create gists. `solve --log-dir` now actually writes the session log into that directory. The default Agent model moves from the withdrawn `opencode/nemotron-3-super-free` to `kilo/nemotron-3-super-free`. Result verification works with integration tokens and prints the real failure reason. Command-stream is bumped to 2.0.0 and Sentry to 11.5.0.
diff --git a/.github/workflows/release.yml b/.github/workflows/release.yml
index 9f3863de5..5318ccad1 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/release.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/release.yml
@@ -22,9 +22,14 @@ on:
         type: choice
         default: 'checks'
         options: [checks, instant, changeset-pr]
+      # Issue #2625: a required input without a default makes GitHub refuse
+      # every API dispatch that omits it (HTTP 422 "Required input 'bump_type'
+      # not provided"), including the `mode=checks` dispatch of
+      # scripts/dispatch-checks.mjs. `patch` is what the web form preselects.
       bump_type:
         description: 'Manual release type'
         required: true
+        default: patch
         type: choice
         options:
           - patch
@@ -84,6 +89,9 @@ jobs:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v7
         with:
           fetch-depth: 0
+      # Issue #2625: freshness blocks pull requests only (#2264). On a push to
+      # main it warns, so a release published after a merge cannot skip the
+      # tests and the release of code that already passed the gate.
       - name: Verify dependency freshness and detect changes
         id: changes
         env:
